"**Former Vice\u2011Presidents who ran for president & won (as of 2024)**  \n\n| VP\u2011turned\u2011President | Military service |\n|----------------------|------------------|\n| **Thomas Jefferson** | Virginia Militia (Colonel, 1775\u20131776 \u2013 American Revolutionary War) |\n| **Martin\u202fVan\u202fBuren** | New\u202fYork (Albany County) Militia (Captain, Revolutionary War) |\n| **Richard\u202fNixon** | United States Navy Reserve (Lieutenant\u2011Commander, 1947\u20131949; served as a medical officer) |\n| **Theodore\u202fRoosevelt** | United States Army (New\u202fYork National Guard officer \u2192 U.S. Volunteer Cavalry, Spanish\u2011American War) |\n| **Harry\u202fS.\u202fTruman** | United States Army (First Lieutenant, World War\u202fI \u2013 personal\u2011service, no combat) |\n| **Lyndon\u202fB.\u202fJohnson** | United States Navy Reserve (Lieutenant\u2011Commander, 1941\u20131942 \u2013 naval observer, WWII) |\n| **George\u202fH.\u202fW.\u202fBush** | United States Navy (Naval aviator, 1942\u20131945 \u2013 171 combat missions, World War\u202fII) |\n\n**Answer**\n\n- **7 former Vice Presidents** who ran for president and won had some form of military service.  \n- Their branches of service were: **Virginia militia**, **New\u202fYork militia**, **U.S. Navy Reserve** (twice), **U.S. Army** (twice), and **U.S. Navy**."